WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Start with today's manual workflow. People
copy cases, prepare shared accounts,

00:00:04.768 --> 00:00:08.240
wait for a vendor test slot,
and reconcile screenshots and logs.

00:00:08.411 --> 00:00:12.840
Seventy-five testers still face
the same environment bottleneck.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.360
Now separate the modernization step.

00:00:15.456 --> 00:00:18.560
Engineers create reviewed automated tests,

00:00:18.622 --> 00:00:22.440
isolated data, and validated
simulations of the payment provider.

00:00:22.570 --> 00:00:26.880
The delivery pipeline runs those
tests and retains the evidence.

00:00:26.976 --> 00:00:29.760
That repeatability is
valuable even without AI.

00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:33.040
Real-provider checks still
need vendor capacity.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:38.960
Then add AI assistance. It helps
draft cases, test code and fixtures,

00:00:39.004 --> 00:00:43.200
recommends relevant coverage, and helps
explain failures and summarize proof.

00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:48.240
Engineers review the outputs,
existing runners execute, and people make

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.200
release decisions. Compare equivalent
payment packs at all three stages.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:58.080
Measure waiting and reliability
separately from AI drafting, review

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:03.440
and rework. These are proposed states,
not measured client improvements.
